WEBVTT

00:10:28.324 --> 00:10:32.429
And you know, that becomes
an exercise in frustration.

00:10:32.453 --> 00:10:34.429
AG: In other words, that's a nice theory

00:10:34.453 --> 00:10:36.564
about encouraging
everyone to keep producing

00:10:36.588 --> 00:10:38.190
at maximum capacity for decades,

00:10:38.214 --> 00:10:39.619
but it might not be realistic

00:10:39.643 --> 00:10:41.611
if you're not a superstar in your field.

00:10:41.635 --> 00:10:45.054
The rest of us are going to do
what people naturally do.

00:10:45.078 --> 00:10:48.611
And Arthur wants there to be space
for that path, too.

00:10:48.635 --> 00:10:51.346
He wants people to be excellent
in their own way,

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:53.641
which made me wonder
if he thinks career decline

00:10:53.665 --> 00:10:56.227
is more inevitable for people
who achieve excellence.

00:10:56.654 --> 00:10:58.916
AB: What goes up
must come down ultimately,

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.261
and the higher up you go,